# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore — triad-audit
#
# Two jobs, and they are different jobs:
#
#   1. THIS FILE excludes things by PATH and NAME.
#   2. tools/check_no_leaks.py excludes things by CONTENT.
#
# A .gitignore pattern cannot see inside a file.  It cannot tell that a
# perfectly ordinary filename contains a forbidden identifier in its text.
# So this file is not the content guard, and it is not the primary guard for
# identifier-shaped filenames either -- see the note in section 2.
# Run the scanner.  Both exist because either alone is a false sense of
# safety.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Local-only configuration
#
# .leaks.local holds the actual identifier list the scanner uses.  It is
# untracked on purpose: an enforcement mechanism that spells out the
# identifier it protects has leaked it.  A pattern like "*<token>*" written
# here would publish the token just as surely as prose would.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.leaks.local
*.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Enforcement by name
#
# Deliberately EMPTY of literal tokens.  Whatever the audited stack is called,
# that string does not appear in this repository -- not in a pattern, not in
# a comment, not in a docstring explaining the rule.  The name-level check
# therefore lives in the [path] section of .leaks.local, and is applied by
# tools/check_no_leaks.py before a commit.
#
# This is a real trade: a .gitignore pattern fires even if the scanner is
# never run, whereas this arrangement depends on the scanner being run.  It
# is worth it, because a guard that leaks the secret it guards is not a guard.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Withheld artifacts (Appendix A of the manuscript)
#
# Appendix A publishes these two artifacts BY SIZE AND DIGEST ONLY:
#
#   frozen scoring stack (serialised)      212717 B   2db0c9f622f79fb0
#   branch structure and response surface    12.2 KB   6f7449ec02af1f19
#
# "Withheld means not published; it does not mean that no such file exists."
#
# Unlike section 2, these name patterns leak nothing: the artifact names are
# already published in the manuscript.  They are excluded by name fragment
# AND by serialisation type, because the exact filenames are not part of the
# published record.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
frozen_stack*
*frozen*scoring*
*scoring*stack*
response_surface*
branch_structure*
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.npz
*.npy
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.parquet
*.feather

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Raw workspace material
#
# The audit ran over a working tree containing inputs, outputs and logs from
# the audited pipeline.  Those are not part of this repository: they are the
# material the audit was performed ON, and shipping them would publish the
# thing the paper only describes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
raw/
raw_*
workspace/
_pod_fetch*/
artifacts/
data/raw/
inputs/
outputs/
logs/
*.jsonl
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Scratch and probe scripts
#
# Probe scripts are how a claim was checked, not what is being released.
# They stay in the working tree, never committed; released tooling lives
# under tools/ and is written to stand on its own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
_scratch/
_*.py
_probe_*
_tmp*
scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Build residue
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
build/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Machine-specific
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.venv/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
